          "filename": "Hawk XX315 at Manston 1986 (52095781434).jpg",
          "caption": "Royal Air Force (RAF) BAe Hawk T.1 XX315 from No. 1 Tactical Weapons Unit (1TWU) at RAF Brawdy.  The unit moved to RAF Valley when Brawdy closed in 1992, and XX315 joined No. 4 Flying Training School (4FTS) there.  It was loaned to the Royal Navy (RN) FRADU at RNAS Yeovilton in 1995, and returned to RAF 4FTS at Valley in 2001.  It eventually went into store at RAF Shawbury in 2016.  Photo: Dick Gilbert, RAF Manston 70th Anniversary Open Day, 31 May 1986.",
          "alt": "Royal Air Force (RAF) BAe Hawk T.1 XX315 from No. 1 Tactical Weapons Unit (1TWU) at RAF Brawdy.  The unit moved to RAF Valley when Brawdy closed in 1992, and XX315 joined No. 4 Flying Training School (4FTS) there.  It was loaned to the Royal Navy (RN) FRADU at RNAS Yeovilton in 1995, and returned to RAF 4FTS at Valley in 2001.  It eventually went into store at RAF Shawbury in 2016.  Photo: Dick Gilbert, RAF Manston 70th Anniversary Open Day, 31 May 1986.",
